 die to stop the world  from ending but unlike his childhood dog  tally he doesn't crawl off to be alone  instead he returns to his family home  dying to save his parents sisters  Gretchen and everyone else he cares  about the most the existential despair  at the idea of dying alone is only  troubling insofar as human connect  action Gives Life Meaning even in her  Madness and Decades of fear driven by  glimpses of the true nature of time and  the universe Roberta Sparrow still  checks her mail every day hoping for  someone to reach out the spears or  vectors emanating from people's chests  that Dani begins to see are a way for  the movie to address an inevitable  Paradox that any time travel flick runs  into free will if you can see your  future it stands to reason that you  would have the option to change it  Donnie follows his own Spirit to the gun  hidden in his parents closet but it's  not until much later that we learn he  chooses to take it with him later  looking at aggression spear he seems to  get a whole dose of her future in a  Flash and so he rushes to Roberta  Sparrow's house Donnie seems content to  operate within God's Channel as he puts  it to Dr monotov and follow his glimpses  of the future wherever they lead he does  seem surprised when the journey to  Roberto Sparrow's Cellar inadvertently  leads to Gretchen's death because he  shoots Frank retaliation with his  parents gun his motivations are as  unclear as the Paradox of Free Will in  the abstract are we the architects of  our own fate or are we just following a  path that we can't see  Donny's English teacher Miss Pomeroy  plays a small but key role in the  climactic events of the movie as the  phrase Cellar Door leads Donnie and  Gretchen to their Fateful Encounter With  the school bullies somewhat randomly  Miss Pomeroy writes the words on her  chalkboard inspired by a quote famous  linguist who claimed it was the most  beautiful phrase in the English language  that famous linguist was in fact the  Lord of the Rings author J.R.R Tolkien  it's a relatively absurd connection and  the artificiality of it is driven home  explicitly when Donnie mumbles a certain  phrase while fighting  deus ex machina refers to a random and  unlikely act occurring in a story  usually to save the protagonist from  certain Peril Donnie seems at least  subconsciously aware that the entire  last month of his life is one endless  deus ex machina all of these unlikely  events are conspiring to achieve a  certain world saving result the reason  Frank has Donnie burned down Jim  Cunningham is one of the more difficult  things to parse in Donnie Darko  according to Roberto Sparrow Frank is  setting an insurance trap to make sure  that Donnie goes through with his  self-sacrifice since Mrs farmer ends up  spearheading Cunningham's defense  efforts she can't accompany the dance  team's Sparkle motion when they get on  Star Search in Los Angeles for this  reason Donny's mother Rose goes instead  as an indirect result of all this  switching the team takes a red-eye  flight back instead of waiting until the  next day so this ensures that Donny's  mother and younger sister will be on the  very plane that loses an engine in  addition to preventing Gretchen's death  Donnie must also reset the timeline to  save his mother and sister this hits a  little harder since he only got to know  Gretchen as a result of Frank's  instruction to flood the school to begin  with  shortly before the dramatic events of  Halloween night Donnie writes Roberto  Sparrow a long awaited letter even  though he marks the envelope extremely  important the letter doesn't really seem  all that time sensitive he says  cryptically that he has lots of  questions for her that he's afraid to  know the answers to the letter ends with  a morbidly optimistic phrase I hope that  when the world comes to an end  I can breathe a sigh of relief  because there will be so much to look  forward to this observation indicates  that he'